## Wisp Forge's own pixel font (user, 21 Nov: a pixel-art UI): a proportional bitmap face, caps 7 pixels
## tall, lowercase 5, descenders 2, built at start-up into a FontFile (`make`, `make(true)` for the bold
## headings: every pixel doubled to its right). Its size is `SIZE` (10: 8 above the baseline, 2 below);
## used at a whole multiple of it (ui.gd `fsize`), it stays crisp: one font pixel is that many screen pixels.
## GLYPHS: character -> [the row its first line is on (0 = the top of a capital), its rows]. A new character
## is one line here.
extends RefCounted

const SIZE := 10
const ASCENT := 8
const DESCENT := 2

